            <ArticleTitle>Uterine leiomyoma as a rare cause of acute abdomen and intestinal gangrene.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>830-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A rare case of mesenteric vein thrombosis and small intestinal gangrene caused by a pedunculated fundal uterine fibroid is presented. The causative mechanism and management are discussed.</AbstractText>
